<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch May consumer spending rises 3.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch May consumer spending rises 3.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch consumer spending rose 3.6 percent in volume terms in May compared with May 1996, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p> DUTCH CONSUMER SPENDING	 May 97  April 97   May 96</p>
<p>yr-on-yr pct volume changes</p>
<p> Total consumer spending	 3.6	3.7	 4.4</p>
<p>  - food, beverages, tobacco   4.8	3.4	10.3</p>
<p>  - durable goods		  2.9	3.4	 5.8</p>
<p>  - other goods and services   3.5	3.8	 2.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Consumer spending rose by 3.1 percent year-on-year over the first five months of 1997, CBS said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
